  (141,3,$q$The Panthers won exactly 2 of their first 9 games. They then won all of their remaining N games, and finished having won exactly half of all the games they played. What is N?$q$,1,array['Set 1']::text[],'apsmo',null,'S1-3C'),
  (141,4,$q$When Mrs Murphy puts her class into groups of 4, 1 student is left over. In groups of 5, 2 are left over. What is the smallest possible class size?$q$,3,array['Set 1']::text[],'apsmo',null,'S1-3D'),
  (141,5,$q$If 16 is added to one-third of a number, the result is three times the number. What is the number?$q$,2,array['Set 1']::text[],'apsmo',null,'S1-3E'),
  (141,6,$q$Find the whole number N if N = ½ of ⅔ of ¾ of ⅘ of 100.$q$,1,array['Set 1']::text[],'apsmo',null,'S1-4A'),
